{
  "description": "Golden Board order (Story 3.1; regenerated 2026-10-21 for Needs you alone on top and every other class grouped by workspace, ranked Working 1, Finished 2, Idle 3, Unknown 4; regenerated again 2026-10-21 for Background, ranked 2 between Working and Finished, which moves Finished to 3, Idle to 4 and Unknown to 5; regenerated a third time 2026-10-21 for the operator's order inside a workspace group, ranked Finished 1, Idle 2, Background 3, Working 4, Unknown 5, each class most recent first, so a zone-1 start is the negated since; Needs you stays longest-waiting first). input holds shuffled Agent inputs, each with view: the expected AgentView exactly as NewAgentView serialises it (key, class, heading, shortened directory, context line, recap, waiting_since, waiting_exact, background, sort_key). order is the expected AgentKey strings after sorting; headers are the indexes, in sorted order, where a zone-1 workspace group starts. Shared fixture: the Go test in internal/core/view_test.go checks every view, the order and the headers; the Board's ordering tests (Story 3.7) sort the expected views by their sort_key arrays, compared element by element, and must not re-derive class, zone, group, rank or sentinels. An unknown group or start is 9007199254740991 (Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER). workspace_id is PaneContext.WorkspaceID (added 2026-10-23, Story 5.13): a lower-zone Agent whose workspace herdr did not position (workspace_position 0) gets its workspace's own group, 2^52 plus the id's 64-bit FNV-1a hash modulo 2^52-1, after every positioned group and before SortUnknown, so w7:p1 (labelled scratch) and w8:p1 (no label) each start their own header; w9:p1 has no workspace id, so its group is still SortUnknown, last. w8:p1's pane title holds U+202E, which the Context Line drops, and w7:p1's session name starts with \"- \", which it keeps. background is AgentViewInput.Background, the process read's verdict, which the view shows only for a done or idle Agent of a program with a rule. tasks are background subagent ids the Agent's transcript shows open and turn_ended whether its main turn ended (ADR-0009, added 2026-10-21): with tasks open a working Agent is Background, ranked 3, when its turn ended, and Working with background_tasks otherwise; background_tasks counts the open tasks plus one for the process read's verdict when no open task is a background command (every tasks id here is a subagent's, so an open command is not expressed). recap is the latest session recap the Agent's transcript shows (ADR-0010, added 2026-10-22): the view carries it unchanged as recap, \"\" when none, and it changes no other value; w1:p2 has one. since is FoldResult.Since (absent: fold not known); exact says the class began live. seen is AgentViewInput.Seen, the operator's acknowledgement of the Agent's current finish (ADR-0014, added 2026-10-27, Story 6.1), absent when false: the view's seen is set only with class finished, which it leaves finished, and a seen Agent that is not Background ranks 2 with Idle, most recent first; workspace docs (w4) holds a Finished Agent w4:p1, a seen one w4:p2 (finished, Status idle, so done to idle within the finish keeps it) and an older Idle one w4:p3, so the seen Box sits between them. Every view carries seen.",
